# GitHub Issues

When the user asks to **create**, **file**, **open**, or **track** a GitHub Issue (or supplies title/body for that purpose):

- Follow `python/rp_app/ARCHITECTURE.md` **§B.1** for `gh issue create`, auth checks, and when *draft-only* is enough.
- Use **§C–§F** in the same file for labels, issue body template, suspected layer, and title prefixes.

If the user explicitly wants a **draft only**, skip `gh` and provide markdown following **§D–§F**.
